(*
porta space-sync — A FULL TIMER TABLE AT THE PUSH LEG'S RE-ARM DOES NOT STRAND THE
BRIDGE (rete#440 R2, review of #470; #81 makes a full table raise in the arming job).

The pull leg's budget lapses: its one-shot has fired, so `cancelBudget` frees nothing
in the reaction that re-arms for the push. Here every slot is taken between the fire
and that reaction, so `timers after:` raises `timer table full` inside `pushStart`.
Before the guard the raise left the bridge in #pulling with no budget armed and no
doorbell coming — a check-in ignored forever. Now the exchange leaves.

What is asserted, and why each is falsifiable:

- `stranded false idle true` — the raise ended the exchange instead of leaving it in
  #pulling.
- `finished 1 sent 1` — leaving said so once, and no PUSH went out without a budget.
- `retry sent 2 pulling true` — with a slot freed, the next check-in starts a new
  exchange: the bridge is not wedged.
expect:
full true
stranded false idle true
finished 1 sent 1
retry sent 2 pulling true
*)
class CheckInTableFull packageUsing: manifest = () (

  public class FakeSocket = ( | private sends ::= 0. | ) (
    public doorbell = ( ^ 'test/net' )
    public sends = ( ^ sends )
    public sendTo: host port: p data: bytes = ( sends:: sends + 1. ^ self )
    public receive = ( ^ nil )
  ) : ()

  public main: platform args: args = (
    | space timers bridge sock finished filler ch r toks n |
    space:: platform space.
    timers:: platform timers.
    space whenever: 'sys/timer' do: [ :t | timers dispatch: t ].
    finished:: 0.
    (space channel: 'sys/porta/exchange') whenever: '' do: [ :v | finished:: finished + 1 ].
    space put: 'obs/health' value: 11.
    sock:: FakeSocket new.
    bridge:: platform PortaBridge socket: sock space: space id: 'n1' peer: '::1' port: 6969
      spans: platform Spans new timers: timers.

    bridge checkIn.
    platform advanceMillis: 2000.        (* the pull budget fires; its post waits in the space *)

    (* Take every slot before the bridge's budget reaction runs. *)
    ch:: space channel: 'test/fill'.
    toks:: platform OrderedCollection new.
    r:: nil. n:: 0.
    [ r == nil and: [ n < 1000 ] ] whileTrue: [
      n:: n + 1.
      r:: platform protectedFire: [ :v | toks add: (timers every: 100000 post: #x on: ch) ] value: nil ].
    ('full ' , (r == nil) not printString) println.

    space drain.                         (* the lapse: a miss, then the push leg's re-arm *)
    ('stranded ' , (bridge state = #pulling) printString , ' idle ' , (bridge state = #idle) printString) println.
    ('finished ' , finished printString , ' sent ' , sock sends printString) println.

    timers cancel: (toks at: 1).
    bridge checkIn.
    ('retry sent ' , sock sends printString , ' pulling ' , (bridge state = #pulling) printString) println.
    ^ 0
  )
) : (
  public packageUsing: manifest = ( ^ self new )
)
